**An Intelligent Treadmill and Its Control Method**

An intelligent treadmill comprises a treadmill body and an intelligent speed control system. The treadmill body incorporates a treadmill deck and a motor, wherein the treadmill deck is divided into an acceleration section, a holding section, and a deceleration section. The intelligent speed control system consists of a gravity-center sensing device, a processor module, a motor driver, and a host computer. The gravity-center sensing device comprises a plurality of infrared array sensors and is sequentially connected to the processor module, the motor driver, and the host computer, with the motor driver being further connected to the motor.

A method for controlling the intelligent treadmill comprises the following steps:

Step 1: The user sets the upper and lower limit values defining the position of the holding section;

Step 2: The user sets a speed adjustment ratio value;

Step 3: The position of the center of gravity of the human body is acquired;

Step 4: Whether the center of gravity of the human body lies within the holding section is detected;

Step 5: Whether the center of gravity of the human body lies within the acceleration section is detected;

Step 6: The processor module detects whether the center of gravity of the human body lies within the deceleration section.

This system enables the user to control the treadmill speed in a swift and intelligent manner, thereby affording a greater sense of safety and stability throughout the course of exercise.
